Subject: mod_fastcgi: call log_err_multiline() rather than the compat alias

log.h keeps log_error_multiline as an object-like alias for the
variadic macro log_err_multiline ("backwards compat for historic
log_error_multiline()").  VSI C miscounts the arguments when the alias
is followed by an argument list containing BUF_PTR_LEN() (which expands
to two arguments): %CC-W-TOOMANYACTLS, then a syntax error.  Calling
log_err_multiline() directly, as the rest of the tree does, avoids it.

--- a/src/mod_fastcgi.c
+++ b/src/mod_fastcgi.c
@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@
 				buffer * const tb = r->tmp_buf;
 				buffer_clear(tb);
 				fastcgi_get_packet_body(tb, hctx, &packet);
-				log_error_multiline(r->conf.errh, __FILE__, __LINE__,
+				log_err_multiline(r->conf.errh, __FILE__, __LINE__,
 				  BUF_PTR_LEN(tb), "FastCGI-stderr:");
 			}
 			break;
